    "narrative": "The primary objective today for Ghost Ride the WHIP is capitalizing on stolen base upside against exploitable rotations, where **Jose Caballero** (80.26) and **Corbin Carroll** (78.36) stand out as our elite plays. **Jose Caballero** benefits from a massive 13% boost due to a dynamic platoon edge against Corbin, while **Corbin Carroll** remains a core anchor despite facing Abbott; his high-floor speed profile against a sub-5.00 xERA arm provides the exact offensive ceiling we require. Similarly, **Tyler Soderstrom** (71.84) and **Josh Naylor** (72.21) are high-leverage starts, with **Tyler Soderstrom** surging thanks to an anticipated cleanup role and a favorable matchup against Sugano.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Travis Bazzana**, who narrowly missed the cut at 49.36. While his lead-off spot provided a +10% efficiency bump, the matchup against Mize\u2014a pitcher with a 3.68 xERA\u2014depressed his overall score compared to our middle-order starters. We are opting to prioritize the higher-upside matchups in the current lineup configuration. However, we remain cautious regarding **Seiya Suzuki** (45.89), whose score is suppressed by Logan Webb\u2019s elite pitching profile and a potential sub-50 output. We are also closely monitoring the lineup statuses for **Max Muncy**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Tyler Soderstrom**; if their projected spots shift, we may lose the calculated efficiency gains currently bolstering their scores. With **Mickey Moniak**, **Trevor Story**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** sidelined on the IL, our depth is thin, making the production from **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland** critical to maintaining our category leads.",
